<title>USA: Documents, witnesses issues in Miss. tobacco case.</title>
<headline>Documents, witnesses issues in Miss. tobacco case.</headline>
<dateline>PASCAGOULA, Miss. 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lawyers representing the tobacco industry on Wednesday argued that the state of Mississippi had systematically refused to hand over information needed to prepare for the industry's defense against a landmark lawsuit.</p>
<p>State lawyers countered that they were cooperating but demands by tobacco companies had become overly burdensome and unreasonable.</p>
<p>Tobacco attorneys on Wednesday asked Jackson County Chancery Judge William Myers to force the state to provide:</p>
